lator Home 5 Total Compensation Calculator Total Compensation Calculator As an Illinois employee, your total compensation package goes beyond just your base salary. You have access to a wide range of benefits, services, and paid leave. To help you understand the value of your compensation, Illinois Human Resources has developed an interactive Total Compensation Calculator. This tool provides a detailed overview based on your employment classification and base salary. The Total Compensation Calculator includes employer contributions from the university but does not account for your portion of self-selected voluntary benefits such as vision insurance, supplemental life insurance, short/long-term disability, and supplemental retirement plans. This tool is useful for both current employees and prospective candidates. To estimate your total compensation package, please make your selections from the dropdowns below. IVP Total Compensation Calculator Tell us about yourself: Academic Professional (AP) Faculty Civil Service Base Annual Salary ($): Look up your salary at MyUIInfo Select Work Week: 40-hour week (2080 hours/year) 37.5-hour week (1950 hours/year) Hourly Rate ($): Look up your hourly rate SURS Retirement Plan Traditional or Portable (11.98% of base annual salary) Retirement Savings Plan (RSP) (7.60% of base annual salary) Do you have Health, Life, and Dental insurance through the University? Yes ($35,526 flat rate) No Are you taking any credit-based classes at the university? No Tuition Waiver Undergraduate – 6 credit hours ($4,331 per semester) Undergraduate – 12 credit hours ($6,496 per semester) Graduate – 6 credit hours ($4,825 per semester) Graduate – 12 credit hours ($7,237 per semester) * Tuition waivers above $5,250 per year are considered taxable income. Calculate * This tool is for illustrative purposes only. Actual total compensation may vary. For retirement-related calculations, please visit the SURS website . This tool is for illustrative purposes only an provides benefits-eligible employees an estimate of their total compensation based on specific options selected by the employee. Therefore, the actual value of total compensation may be different. Illinois Human Resources Follow Follow Follow Follow Personnel Services Building – MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr., Champaign, IL 61820 Phone: 217-333-2137 Email: ihr@illinois.edu Hours of Operations Monday – Friday: 8:30 A.M. – 12:00 P.M., 1:00 P.M. – 5:00 P.M. Resources About Campus Holiday Schedule Site navigation help Jobs.illinois.edu HR Collaborative MyUInfo Connect Are you a Job Seeker? Who is my unit HR Contact? General HR Questions? Want to share website feedback? If you have difficulty accessing this site, please contact IHR Marketing & Communications for assistance. Explore Campus University Admissions Careers at Illinois University News Visit Campus Connect with Illinois University Alumni Giving at Illinois University Calendars University Directory Access University Resources Emergency Services McKinley Health Center Connie Frank CARE Center University Library About Cookies Privacy Copyright Accessibility"
