    "https://humanresources.illinois.edu/ai-professional-development-series/": {
      "title": "Strategic Programs & Partnerships",
      "description": "AI Professional Development Series | Illinois Human Resources Block I logo UNIVERSITY OF ILLINOIS URBANA-CHAMPAIGN Jobs | Holiday Schedule | About Illinois Human Resources Search for: MENU Job Seekers Job Seekers Job Postings Why Work at Illinois Executive Level Positions Extra Help Services Quick Links Illinois Value Proposition How to Apply Instructions Our Community Benefits & Well-Being Benefits Benefits Chart Total Compensation Calculator Well-Being Work Well Spotlight Focusing Amidst Distractions Quick Links Counseling Services Workplace Flexibility Crisis Support My Employee Experience Illinois Value Proposition IVP Builder IVP Resources IVP Engagement New Employee Onboarding Orientation Resources Workplace Flexibility The Illinois Professional Current Employees Learning & Development Engagement Opportunities Performance Management Recognition Leaving the University Quick Links AI Professional Development Series Benefits Chart HR Career Architecture Pay & Time-Entry Resources Policies A-Z New Supervisor Resources Services & Information Services Service Center Matrix Teams Learning & Development Employee Relations (LER) Consulting (ELOE) Counseling & Well-Being Resources Information Forms Job Aids HR Applications Pay & Time-Entry Resources HR Document Library Processes Hiring Employees Performance Management Promotion / Reclassification Time Reporting Separations Leaves Policies A-Z Index Quick Links AI Professional Development Series Civil Service Salary Plan HR Collaborative JDXpert Service Catalog About Centers of Expertise Compensation, Classification & Career Architecture HR Applications & Information Services HR Data Operations Labor & Employee Relations Matrix Teams Talent Culture, Learning & Engagement Employee Engagement & Recognition Employee Learning & Organizational Effectiveness Faculty/Staff Assistance and Well-Being Services Strategic Programs & Partnerships HR Analytics About Administration Policy Design & Administration Meet Our Staff/Directory Organizational Structure IHR By the Numbers Contact Us Search for: Job Seekers Job Seekers Job Postings Why Work at Illinois Executive Level Positions Extra Help Services Quick Links Illinois Value Proposition How to Apply Instructions Our Community Benefits & Well-Being Benefits Benefits Chart Total Compensation Calculator Well-Being Work Well Spotlight Focusing Amidst Distractions Quick Links Counseling Services Workplace Flexibility Crisis Support My Employee Experience Illinois Value Proposition IVP Builder IVP Resources IVP Engagement New Employee Onboarding Orientation Resources Workplace Flexibility The Illinois Professional Current Employees Learning & Development Engagement Opportunities Performance Management Recognition Leaving the University Quick Links AI Professional Development Series Benefits Chart HR Career Architecture Pay & Time-Entry Resources Policies A-Z New Supervisor Resources Services & Information Services Service Center Matrix Teams Learning & Development Employee Relations (LER) Consulting (ELOE) Counseling & Well-Being Resources Information Forms Job Aids HR Applications Pay & Time-Entry Resources HR Document Library Processes Hiring Employees Performance Management Promotion / Reclassification Time Reporting Separations Leaves Policies A-Z Index Quick Links AI Professional Development Series Civil Service Salary Plan HR Collaborative JDXpert Service Catalog About Centers of Expertise Compensation, Classification & Career Architecture HR Applications & Information Services HR Data Operations Labor & Employee Relations Matrix Teams Talent Culture, Learning & Engagement Employee Engagement & Recognition Employee Learning & Organizational Effectiveness Faculty/Staff Assistance and Well-Being Services Strategic Programs & Partnerships HR Analytics About Administration Policy Design & Administration Meet Our Staff/Directory Organizational Structure IHR By the Numbers Contact Us Strategic Programs & Partnerships AI Professional Development Series Home 5 AI Professional Development Series AI Professional Development Series Thriving in a Dynamic Workplace The way we work is changing rapidly. Emerging technologies, evolving roles, and shifting priorities make the workplace more dynamic than ever. To succeed, employees and leaders need the skills, confidence, and mindset to help navigate change effectively. Our future-forward professional development initiatives help you stay agile, understand key nuances for informed decision-making, and thrive in this type of evolving environment. In a dynamic workplace, change is constant and adaptability comes to the forefront. Being adaptable means not only responding to new tools and processes but it also helps individuals anticipate and shape what’s on the horizon. The following professional development series is driven by the Illinois Human Resources and the Office of the Chief Information Officer . We are pleased to be partnering with CITL, the Library, and other key partners in this effort. Artificial Intelligence (AI) Professional Development Series The AI upskilling initiative is designed to help staff and leaders develop the real-world skills needed to work smarter, adapt faster, and collaborate effectively with AI tools. Each learning pathway builds confidence and capability, starting with foundational literacy and moving toward applied and advanced skills. This helps build a more adaptive, innovative, and AI-confident workforce prepared for the next era of work. The overarching initiative goals are to build an AI‑enabled workforce and leadership culture, accelerate organizational readiness for AI‑driven transformation, strengthen internal talent mobility through future‑relevant career pathways, and foster responsible, ethical, and human‑centered AI adoption across the university. The key objectives of this series are to develop future‑ready AI skills, build departmental champions, strengthen organizational adaptability, and support responsible, ethical AI‑driven decision‑making. View detailed key objectives and overarching initiative goals Staff Series  Foundational  Intermediate  Advanced  Unit AI Explorer This level builds awareness, confidence, and responsible use of AI at work. It introduces key mindsets, simple workflows, ethical guardrails, and practical ways AI reshapes tasks. Participants learn to stay adaptable, experiment safely, and use basic AI-assisted actions in daily work. Participants Gain A baseline understanding of what AI can and cannot do. Safe and ethical usage principles. Intro-level examples of AI in workflows. Modules Getting Started with AI: What’s All the Hype? - Demystify AI, its role, and its impact on work. Human-Machine Teaming - Explore practical collaboration models and teaming strategies. Prompt Engineering (AI Fluency) - Learn how to craft effective AI prompts for better results. Safe Experimentation with AI - Understand risks, safety guidelines, and responsible use. Learning in the Flow in Work - Integrate AI learning naturally into daily tasks. AI in My Workday - Building an AI Ready Mindset - Integrates AI into daily work while fostering adaptability and continuous learning. AI Catalyst – Registration Now Available! This level builds practical skills with approved AI tools and helps employees understand when to rely on AI and when human judgment is needed. It emphasizes hands-on practice, role‑specific use cases, and developing confidence using AI for everyday tasks—without requiring technical expertise. Participants Gain Ability to choose when to use AI and when human oversight remains critical. Confidence in using AI for everyday tasks, such as summaries, drafting, organization, data prep, etc. Clarity on how AI fits into their specific role level and responsibilities. Program Structure The Intermediate Level consists of two components: Part 1 : Participants will focus on specific usage of an AI tool (e.g., Microsoft Copilot, ChatGPT, Google Gemini, Illinois Chat, or Zoom AI Companion). On-demand courses are available for Microsoft Copilot, ChatGPT, and Google Gemini). Microsoft Copilot Deep Dive ChatGPT Deep Dive Google Gemini Deep Dive Part 2 : This session focuses on learning how to further leverage AI tools in your current position. You will select one of the available scenarios and work through that scenario with peers in similar roles. Key Outcomes Demonstrate proficiency with common AI tools and features in existing software. Understand AI’s strengths, limitations, and how it applies to specific roles and responsibilities. Evaluate when to use AI and when human oversight or judgement is critical, and how AI can support daily tasks. Upcoming Part 2 Sessions All sessions below are the same, so you only need to sign up for one option . Monday, July 27, 2026 9:00 a.m.–10:30 a.m. | In Person | Nevada Building Computer Lab Monday, August 3, 2026 3:00 p.m.–4:30 p.m. | In Person | Nevada Building Computer Lab Wednesday, September 2, 2026 3:00p.m.–4:30 p.m. | Virtual Friday, September 18, 2026 2:00p.m.–3:30 p.m. | In Person | Nevada Building Computer Lab | Register here Monday, September 21, 2026 10:30 a.m.–12:00 p.m. | Virtual | Register here Monday, October 12, 2026 10:30 a.m.–12:00 p.m. | Virtual | Register here Thursday, November 5, 2026 10:30 a.m.–12:00 p.m. | Virtual | Register here Note: Participating in the Foundational series is not required but recommended. If you have a good working knowledge of a specific AI tool or have taken sessions offered through CITL, the Library, or your unit, you can register for the Intermediate Series. AI Practitioner This level develops advanced, hands‑on AI practitioners who can drive team adoption and workflow improvements. Participants learn to prototype practical AI solutions, evaluate outputs, share expertise, and collaborate across teams to pilot responsible, human‑centered enhancements. At this stage, employees can help their teams work smarter, faster, and more confidently with AI. Participants Gain Deep proficiency using university-approved AI tools, including prompt design, workflow construction, and output evaluation. The capability to assess which tasks can be augmented, and the points that require human oversight. Experience collaborating with team leads or subject-matter experts to pilot small-scale workflow improvements. Unit Training In addition to our individual-focused AI Professional Development Series, we are offering tailored Unit Training sessions to explore ways to collaborate and implement AI that can enhance collective performance, streamline workflow, and foster a shared understanding of AI’s role in your work. Fill out the Interest Form for an AI Unit Training What is Unit Training? It’s a flexible, facilitated experience that helps units: Identify opportunities to apply AI to shared tasks and workflows. Explore university-supported tools, including ChatGPT, Google Gemini, Illinois Chat, Microsoft Copilot Chat, and Notebook LM. Design team-specific AI-supported processes (e.g., content creation, data analysis, meeting summaries, project management, research support). Engage in open discussion about how AI can be effectively leveraged in your area. Establish team norms and best practices for responsible, ethical, and effective AI use. Navigate common challenges, including change management, human oversight, and output verification. Sessions are tailored to your unit’s size, needs, and current level of AI experience. Whether you are just getting stared or looking to deepen integration, Unit Training supports your next stage of adoption. Key Benefits for Unit Collective upskilling: Build shared capability across the team and reduce knowledge gaps. Improved collaboration: Explore how AI can enhance teamwork, communication, and innovation. Actionable outcomes: Leave with practical outputs such as workflows, guidelines, prompt libraries, or pilot ideas that are ready to test. Leadership & culture support: Equip leaders with insights to guide AI adoption while addressing team questions, concerns, and opportunities. Leadership Series  Foundational  Intermediate  Advanced AI Ready Leaders - Coming August 2026 This level builds essential awareness for leaders by helping them understand AI’s practical value, limitations, and implications. Leaders learn how to create conditions for responsible experimentation and support their teams in adopting AI tools with clarity and confidence. Participants Gain A clear understanding of how AI enhances human leadership. Awareness of risks, guardrails, and ethical considerations in a leadership context. A practical framework for guiding teams through AI adoption. Modules AI Fluency for Today's Leaders - Understand AI fundamentals and implications. Human-AI Collaboration in Action - Define roles, workflows, and teaming best practices. Cultivating Trust Amid AI-Driven Change - Learn to foster trust and lead change as teams adapt to AI-enabled collaboration. Responsible AI Leadership - Establish ethical guardrails and safe AI policies. Upskilling for an AI-Ready Workforce - Plan learning lattices and build AI capabilities at scale. The AI Ready Leader - Equip leaders to steer teams through AI-driven change with trust and confidence. AI Adaptive Leaders This level strengthens a leader’s ability to guide change, coach others, and redesign workflows as AI becomes more embedded. Leaders develop practical strategies for decision-making, prioritization, and enabling team growth in a rapidly evolving environment. Participants Gain The ability to coach employees through change fatigue and uncertainty. Strategies for adapting workflows, priorities, and team structures. A leadership approach that integrates human-centered decision-making with AI insights. AI Forward Strategies This level develops leaders who can actively shape organizational transformation. These leaders help with AI strategies, champion cross-functional alignment, and translate emerging technologies into actionable direction. They can anticipate disruption, steward ethical change, and guide teams toward future-ready capabilities. Participants Gain A strategic lens for anticipating how AI reshapes roles, structures, and talent needs. The ability to evaluate and prioritize AI investments aligned to mission and outcomes. Tools to build a culture of experimentation, innovation, and responsible governance. Explore CITL & Library GenAI Resources AI learning is supported through multiple partners across campus. We encourage you to check out other offerings available through CITL, the Library, or your unit. CITL Upcoming Sessions on GenAI Library Guide on Incorporating GenAI Frequently Asked Questions Do you have to attend all of the series? No, you can sign up for each session individually. We understand that everyone is at various stages with their level of understanding and working with AI. This series was designed so that each session builds on each other allowing you to start with whatever session fits your needs. What do you define as a leader for this series? Someone who leads a team of people or who makes decisions for AI-related efforts. Can we receive a badge for this series? Yes, if you attend five of the six sessions in the series. Is it an approved event? The AI Professional Development is an approved event under Policy and Rules for Civil Service Staff, Rule 11.12. Employees can attend with up to two hours off work, pending supervisor approval & operations permitting. Each of session is designed as 90 minutes in length which falls under the two-hour timeframe. Will there be other AI training offered? Depending on campus interest we will repeat these sessions. In addition, we are working on another wave of training that will target more specifics (Copilot, ChatGPT, etc.). We will share more information on that as soon as it’s available. Can I revisit this training if needed? Yes, this will be available on Canvas. We will start work on that soon. How does this differ from other offerings on campus? There are several great offerings available through CITL, the Library, and other resources on campus. Some are focused more on the needs of faculty and students. This AI Professional Development series is focused on employees in order to help understand various tools currently in the marketplace, how they can be leveraged in roles, along with cautionary guidance. We will continue to build other future-focused courses and series. Generative AI Resources – Technology Services The Generative AI Resources provides the university community with listings of approved AI resources, along with privacy and security considerations. Explore Generative AI Resources Read about the Inaugural AI Professional Development Recap  Have questions? Please contact ihr@illinois.edu . We’re here to help. Illinois Human Resources Follow Follow Follow Follow Personnel Services Building – MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr., Champaign, IL 61820 Phone: 217-333-2137 Email: ihr@illinois.edu Hours of Operations Monday – Friday: 8:30 A.M. – 12:00 P.M., 1:00 P.M. – 5:00 P.M. Resources About Campus Holiday Schedule Site navigation help Jobs.illinois.edu HR Collaborative MyUInfo Connect Are you a Job Seeker? Who is my unit HR Contact? General HR Questions? Want to share website feedback? If you have difficulty accessing this site, please contact IHR Marketing & Communications for assistance. Explore Campus University Admissions Careers at Illinois University News Visit Campus Connect with Illinois University Alumni Giving at Illinois University Calendars University Directory Access University Resources Emergency Services McKinley Health Center Connie Frank CARE Center University Library About Cookies Privacy Copyright Accessibility"
    },
