aff/Directory Organizational Structure IHR By the Numbers Contact Us Search for: Job Seekers Job Seekers Job Postings Why Work at Illinois Executive Level Positions Extra Help Services Quick Links Illinois Value Proposition How to Apply Instructions Our Community Benefits & Well-Being Benefits Benefits Chart Total Compensation Calculator Well-Being Work Well Spotlight Focusing Amidst Distractions Quick Links Counseling Services Workplace Flexibility Crisis Support My Employee Experience Illinois Value Proposition IVP Builder IVP Resources IVP Engagement New Employee Onboarding Orientation Resources Workplace Flexibility The Illinois Professional Current Employees Learning & Development Engagement Opportunities Performance Management Recognition Leaving the University Quick Links AI Professional Development Series Benefits Chart HR Career Architecture Pay & Time-Entry Resources Policies A-Z New Supervisor Resources Services & Information Services Service Center Matrix Teams Learning & Development Employee Relations (LER) Consulting (ELOE) Counseling & Well-Being Resources Information Forms Job Aids HR Applications Pay & Time-Entry Resources HR Document Library Processes Hiring Employees Performance Management Promotion / Reclassification Time Reporting Separations Leaves Policies A-Z Index Quick Links AI Professional Development Series Civil Service Salary Plan HR Collaborative JDXpert Service Catalog About Centers of Expertise Compensation, Classification & Career Architecture HR Applications & Information Services HR Data Operations Labor & Employee Relations Matrix Teams Talent Culture, Learning & Engagement Employee Engagement & Recognition Employee Learning & Organizational Effectiveness Faculty/Staff Assistance and Well-Being Services Strategic Programs & Partnerships HR Analytics About Administration Policy Design & Administration Meet Our Staff/Directory Organizational Structure IHR By the Numbers Contact Us New Supervisor Resources New Supervisor Resources Home 5 New Supervisor Resources New Supervisor Resources New Supervisor Resources Welcome to the University of Illinois! As a new supervisor, you play a crucial role in our community. Our onboarding resources are designed to help you succeed in your role and contribute to the university’s mission. We’re excited to have you on board! Collective Bargaining and Grievance Processes Understanding collective bargaining and grievance processes can improve conflict resolution, promote fair treatment, support workers’ rights, and maintain a positive workplace. Collective Bargaining Definition Grievances Policy for Civil Service employees Grievances Process for Academic Professionals Labor Agreements Employment Policies Understanding employment policies ensure legal compliance, help to make informed decisions, and foster a fair, transparent workplace. Alcohol and Drugs Policy Board of Trustees Statutes Flexible work schedules Managing Performance Overtime Policy for Civil Service employees Policies Webpage Postdoc Tax Info Pregnancy and Related Conditions policy Reporting Discrimination, Harassment or Retaliation (OAE) Title IX Office: Sex-Based Misconduct Policy University Code of Conduct University Reporting Policy for Ethics ( SOEEA ) for Civil Service exempt and Academic Professionals employees Hiring and Classification Knowledge of hiring and classification can help to make better informed decisions, ensuring the right candidates are selected for the right roles. This promotes efficiency and employee trust. Departmental Classification Program (DCP) Job Postings Prior Sex-based Misconduct Policy SUCSS Statute and Rules Why Work at Illinois Inclusion and Well-being Understanding inclusion and well-being can create a supportive work environment, leading to higher job satisfaction and team performance. This knowledge helps reduce stress and fosters a culture of respect and innovation. Accessibility and Accommodations AccessLab@Illinois Connect and Engage Digital Accessibility Policy Faculty/Staff Assistance and Well-Being Services Mental Health Resources Shared Benefits Workplace Flexibility Leave Policies Understanding leave policies help reduce misunderstandings and promote employee well-being and cohesion. Approved and unapproved absences for Civil Service employees Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Holiday Policy Paid Leave for All Workers Sick leave for academic staff members Sick Leave for Civil Service and Academic employees Vacation and Personal Leave policy for Civil Service employees Vacation policy for Civil Service and Academic employees Vacation/Sick Leave Reporting Benefits The University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign offers a wide range of exceptional benefits to our employees. Our benefits encompass competitive compensation, comprehensive healthcare coverage, retirement savings plans, and generous time off. We prioritize a flexible workplace that suits your needs. Benefits Fostering a Culture of Respect The Office of the Vice Chancellor for Access, Civil Rights & Community (OVCACRC) is committed to increasing inclusivity in all areas of university life. This includes campus climate surveys, responding to bias incident reports, funding antiracism initiatives, and supporting employee accommodation and accessibility through accommodation requests and access labs. OVCACRC celebrates diversity and campus climate through events, education, training, and funding. Contact: access@illinois.edu OVCACRC Performance Management In the realm of Performance Management, our focus is on supporting the continuous enhancement of individual, team, and organizational performance. We strive to drive future-focused success by leveraging insights from current work to inform strategic planning encompassing goals, accountabilities, inclusion, innovation, and collaboration. Performance Management Public Safety The mission of the Division of Public Safety at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign is to promote a safe and secure environment at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign. Resources include C.O.A.S.T., Campus Violence Prevention Plan, Threat Assessment Protocol, and UIPD. Contact: police@illinois.edu Public Safety Search Process and Recruitment The Office for Access and Equity promotes equal employment opportunity throughout the university’s hiring and personnel processes. Contact: accessandequity@illinois.edu Search Process & Recruitment Separation/ Offboarding When departing the university, employees must adhere to specific processes tailored to their individual circumstances. Whether an employee is leaving due to the conclusion of their appointment, resignation, or retirement, it is crucial to follow the designated procedures. For those eligible for retirement or benefit- or leave-eligible, there are additional considerations. Separation/Offboarding Take a Deeper Dive Enhance your leadership skills and managerial capabilities with our Supervisor Development programs at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. Designed for individuals in supervisory or managerial roles, these programs provide essential training, resources, and support to help supervisors excel and drive team success. New supervisors are encouraged to attend the Human Resources Series for Supervisors and Managers (HR Series), a multi-topic series focused on Illinois Human Resources (IHR) policies and guiding principles providing crucial information to create a positive workforce and productive work environment. This series of seminars is vital to successful supervision and management and are free of charge to employees. Supervisor Development Learning & Development Illinois Human Resources Follow Follow Follow Follow Personnel Services Building – MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr., Champaign, IL 61820 Phone: 217-333-2137 Email: ihr@illinois.edu Hours of Operations Monday – Friday: 8:30 A.M. – 12:00 P.M., 1:00 P.M. – 5:00 P.M. Resources About Campus Holiday Schedule Site navigation help Jobs.illinois.edu HR Collaborative MyUInfo Connect Are you a Job Seeker? Who is my unit HR Contact? General HR Questions? Want to share website feedback? If you have difficulty accessing this site, please contact IHR Marketing & Communications for assistance. Explore Campus University Admissions Careers at Illinois University News Visit Campus Connect with Illinois University Alumni Giving at Illinois University Calendars University Directory Access University Resources Emergency Services McKinley Health Center Connie Frank CARE Center University Library About Cookies Privacy Copyright Accessibility"
    },
